[coal] Give the broadphase callback base classes virtual destructors

CollisionCallBackBase and DistanceCallBackBase are polymorphic bases -- they
exist to be derived from -- but have implicit, non-virtual, public
destructors. Deleting a derived callback through a base pointer is therefore
undefined behavior, and merely deriving from either one is enough to trip
-Wnon-virtual-dtor, which Drake builds with as an error.

Drake will define several such callbacks for its broadphase queries, so the
fix belongs upstream rather than in a suppression at each derived class.

--- include/coal/broadphase/broadphase_callbacks.h
+++ include/coal/broadphase/broadphase_callbacks.h
@@ -47,6 +47,8 @@
 /// according to the application (e.g, only listing the potential
 /// CollisionObjects in collision).
 struct COAL_DLLAPI CollisionCallBackBase {
+  virtual ~CollisionCallBackBase() = default;
+
   /// @brief Initialization of the callback before running the collision
   /// broadphase manager.
   virtual void init() {};
@@ -70,6 +72,8 @@
 /// according to the application (e.g, only listing the potential
 /// CollisionObjects in collision).
 struct COAL_DLLAPI DistanceCallBackBase {
+  virtual ~DistanceCallBackBase() = default;
+
   /// @brief Initialization of the callback before running the collision
   /// broadphase manager.
   virtual void init() {};
